    "reasoning": "All six final answers agree with their own captured MA worked solutions. q-18862: division by (x-2)(x-3) gives x^2+4x+3=(x+1)(x+3). q-112651: (x-5)^2(x^2+9) expands to the given quartic; the source incorrectly writes x-2 instead of x-5 in its second displayed quotient, although its final answer is correct. q-124201: the polar area is (1/2)∫_0^π e^{2θ+2}dθ=e^2(e^{2π}-1)/4. q-3471: the intersection points are (-2,-1/2) and (2/5,5/2), whose coordinates sum to 2/5. q-41957: intersection requires x^2-3x+3=0, whose discriminant is -3; there is no real intersection, so p+q is undefined. Its worked quadratic formula incorrectly uses -3 in the numerator instead of +3, without changing the correct conclusion. q-124166: exactly one intersection requires 16+8k=0, giving k=-2 and the valid intersection (1,2). The three repeated answers remain consistent with the earlier review. No submitted grades are supplied; all MA evidence comes from captured worked solutions. The source_error judgment concerns the authored intermediate errors, not disagreement with the final answers.",
